window.fixiverseLanding=()=>`<div class="learning-more">
<section class="learning-section learning-purpose" id="impact-goal" aria-labelledby="impact-title"><span class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE / OUR HIGH-IMPACT GOAL</span><h2 id="impact-title">Understanding. Confidence.<br>More independence.</h2><p>Built from the experience of tutoring children who need extra support, encouragement and time. Fixiverse gives learners a visible problem they can investigate, repair and explain. Our goal is to help that understanding and confidence carry into the next learning session.</p><div class="impact-goals"><article><span>LEARNING</span><h3>Can they explain a new problem?</h3><p>Record first responses before, after and the next day.</p></article><article><span>CONFIDENCE</span><h3>Do they feel ready to try?</h3><p>Ask the same optional confidence question across sessions.</p></article><article><span>INDEPENDENCE</span><h3>How much coaching is needed?</h3><p>Track interface instructions and math help; keep access accommodations separate.</p></article></div><p class="impact-status"><b>Impact goal, ready to evaluate.</b> The app includes the tutor testing tools. Real learner outcomes still need to be collected; these are the outcomes we aim to improve.</p></section>
<section class="learning-section" aria-labelledby="learning-roles"><div class="learning-section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">ONE NOOK. A LITTLE SUPPORT FOR EVERYONE.</span><h2 id="learning-roles">Small discoveries.<br>A shared picture of learning.</h2><p>Children get room to try. Tutors get the context behind an answer. The next session starts with something useful, not another guess.</p></div><div class="learning-roles">
<article><span class="learning-icon" aria-hidden="true">✧</span><h3>For curious minds</h3><p>Be the person who finds the clue and fixes the machine.</p><ul><li>Build examples you can see</li><li>Compare your idea with Pip’s rule</li><li>Try again with help when you need it</li><li>Become the teacher in Teach Pip</li></ul><button data-hub="fraction">Open Fraction Foundry ↗</button></article>
<article><span class="learning-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</span><h3>For the tutor beside them</h3><p>See what happened, how much help it took, and what to revisit.</p><ul><li>Separate learner profiles</li><li>Guided before, after and next-day tasks</li><li>Interface, math and access support recorded separately</li><li>Calculated results and response exports</li></ul><button data-hub="tutor">Open the tutor workspace ↗</button></article>
<article><span class="learning-icon" aria-hidden="true">♡</span><h3>For their learning team</h3><p>Make the next small step feel manageable.</p><ul><li>Two short, visual missions</li><li>Optional hints and read-aloud</li><li>Pause and return to saved work</li><li>No public scores or leaderboards</li></ul><a href="#how-fixiverse-works">See what’s inside ↓</a></article></div></section>
<section class="learning-section learning-kit" id="how-fixiverse-works" aria-labelledby="learning-inside"><div><span class="eyebrow">WHAT’S INSIDE THE BOOKS</span><h2 id="learning-inside">A little world.<br>Real things to figure out.</h2><p>Each part of Fixiverse connects to something a child or tutor can actually do.</p><dl><div><dt>Fraction Foundry</dt><dd>Build equal-part bars, find a counterexample, and repair Pip’s comparison rule.</dd></div><div><dt>Pattern Grove</dt><dd>Follow a repeating loop and replace the rule that keeps copying the last tile.</dd></div><div><dt>Teach Pip</dt><dd>Choose teaching examples, test Pip on new cases, and inspect which examples changed the possible rules.</dd></div><div><dt>The Rule Lab</dt><dd>Build an executable recipe and check it against a finite collection of examples.</dd></div><div><dt>Tutor testing</dt><dd>Record first responses, confidence, help and access observations in a guided session.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="learning-preview-grid"><figure class="learning-preview fraction-preview"><span class="preview-kicker">01 / FRACTION FOUNDRY</span><h3>One whole.<br>A new way to see it.</h3><div class="preview-whole"><b>½</b><span><i></i><i></i></span></div><div class="preview-whole quarters"><b>¼</b><span><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></div><figcaption>Same-sized wholes. Different-sized pieces.</figcaption></figure><figure class="learning-preview pattern-preview"><span class="preview-kicker">02 / PATTERN GROVE</span><h3>Follow the little loop.</h3><div class="preview-loop" aria-label="Sun, leaf, sun, leaf, missing tile"><span>☀</span><span>❧</span><span>☀</span><span>❧</span><span>?</span></div><figcaption>Notice the rhythm. Start it again.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="learning-section learning-status" aria-labelledby="learning-today"><div><span class="eyebrow">CLEAR ABOUT WHAT’S HERE</span><h2 id="learning-today">Built for trying.<br>Honest about the evidence.</h2><p>The missions, teaching tools and tutor workflow are playable today. The next step is a real tutoring pilot: measure learning, confidence and support needs over time, then improve the app from those observations.</p><button class="learning-cta" data-shelf="tour">Scroll through the learning story ↓</button><p class="learning-fineprint">Tour actions use temporary mission state. Your saved learning records stay separate.</p></div><div class="learning-status-list"><div><i aria-hidden="true">✓</i><span><b>Two visual missions</b><small>Fractions and repeating patterns</small></span><em>Playable</em></div><div><i aria-hidden="true">✓</i><span><b>Teach Pip and the Rule Lab</b><small>Examples, executable rules and inspectable evidence</small></span><em>Playable</em></div><div><i aria-hidden="true">✓</i><span><b>Guided tutoring sessions</b><small>Before, after, next-day and support observations</small></span><em>Available</em></div><div><i aria-hidden="true">✓</i><span><b>Saved work and recovery</b><small>Browser-local profiles, backup and restore</small></span><em>Local</em></div><div><i aria-hidden="true">○</i><span><b>Real learner outcomes</b><small>Collected through voluntary tutoring sessions</small></span><em>To evaluate</em></div></div></section>
<footer class="learning-bottom"><b>fixiverse ✳</b><span>A little curiosity goes a long way.</span><a href="#main">Back to the bookshelf ↑</a><button data-hub="tutor">Tutor workspace ↗</button></footer></div>`;
